<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ziaur Rahman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1936">1936</a>–<a href="/years/1981">1981</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ziaur Rahman was a Bangladeshi army officer who announced the declaration of independence on radio in March 1971 and commanded forces in the Liberation War. After the coups of 1975 he became the country's leading figure and was president from 1977. He founded the Bangladesh Nationalist Party and was assassinated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chittagong">Chittagong</a> in 1981.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ziaur-rahman.jpg" alt="Ziaur Rahman" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kbsBD · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bangladeshi_president_Ziaur_Rahman,_Bir_Uttom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
